  "srp-ocp": `
## SRP
One reason to change = one actor who requests changes.
Tests: one sentence without "and"
who asks for changes?
Employee(pay, hours, save) → PayCalculator, HourReporter, EmployeeRepository.
Not one-method classes: Money(plus, minus, format) is one responsibility.
Opposite smell: shotgun surgery.
## OCP
New case = new class
existing tested code untouched.
DiscountRule interface + injected list in Checkout.
Extension points only where change is likely; rule of three; the prompt tells you.
Prefer interfaces + composition over subclass-and-override.
## Smells
God class; shotgun surgery; speculative generality (one-implementation interfaces "just in case").
`,
  "lsp-isp": `
## LSP
Subtype = promise "treat me as the parent". Keep it.
Rectangle/Square: setWidth must not change height → Square can't comply → use immutable Shape types.
Subtype may: accept more, promise more, keep invariants, no new failure kinds.
Symptoms: throw/no-op overrides, instanceof before calls, "don't call X" comments.
Java: List.copyOf(...).add throws (optional operations).
## ISP
Clients depend only on what they use.
Machine(print, scan, fax) → Printer, Scanner, Fax
classes implement what they can.
Fewer recompiles/retests; tiny fakes; honest promises.
## In LLD answers
One facade is fine, but clients take small interfaces: TicketIssuer, ExitHandler, AvailabilityView.
Not: IOrderService mirroring every method of OrderService.
`,
